UPDATE companies SET description='TZ Medical Inc was founded in 1990 by Tom Tribou in a Portland, Oregon coffee shop. Now headquartered in Tualatin, Oregon, the company began with a two-part philosophy: listen to front-line medical professionals to understand their needs before engineering solutions, and price those solutions at a value level so they reach critical-care providers faster.

Its portfolio includes radial access sheaths such as the Skyline XT™ thin-wall sheath, the Cobra Board radial buttress device, radiation protection systems under the URPro line, cardiac monitoring solutions, the Beata Clasp® medical line organizer, the Pullie™ surgical pannus retractor, anesthesia tube holders, and lead apron racks. Products are sold across the United States and internationally.

TZ Medical serves hospitals, catheterization labs, labor and delivery units, and cardiac monitoring programs. Customers cited in company materials include Abington Jefferson Health, O''Connor Hospital, Providence Newberg Medical Center, The Christ Hospital, and Presence St. Joseph Medical Center in Joliet.

The founding premise remains the company''s stated differentiator: ideas originate from clinicians, not internal engineers alone, and pricing is structured to be accessible without tiered purchasing commitments. The company also emphasizes responsive customer service and tailored account support.', certifications=ARRAY['Joint Commission Telehealth Reaccreditation']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Medical device design and manufacturing", "Radial access sheath production", "Radiation protection system manufacturing", "Cardiac monitoring solution development", "Surgical pannus retraction device manufacturing", "Medical line organizer production", "Anesthesia tube holder manufacturing", "Lead apron storage rack fabrication"], "industries": ["Medical device manufacturing", "Cardiology", "Interventional radiology", "Cardiac monitoring", "Surgical services", "Labor and delivery", "Radiation protection"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Clinician-driven product development: ideas sourced from medical professionals before engineering begins", "Value-based pricing without tiered purchasing commitments", "Responsive, tailored customer support and account management", "Products designed for real clinical workflows", "Nationwide and international distribution"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1990 by Tom Tribou in Portland coffee shop -> /about", "Headquartered in Tualatin, Oregon -> db", "Mission to design, manufacture, deliver medical devices -> /about", "Products: Skyline XT radial sheath, Cobra Board, URPro radiation protection, cardiac monitoring, Beata Clasp, Pullie retractor, anesthesia tube holders, lead apron racks -> /", "Customers: Abington Jefferson Health, O''Connor Hospital, Providence Newberg, Christ Hospital, Presence St. Joe''s Joliet -> /", "Differentiator: clinician-sourced ideas, value pricing, tailored support -> /about, /", "Joint Commission Telehealth Reaccreditation for monitoring solutions -> /", "100 Best Companies to Work for in Oregon awards 2017-2026 -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Our mission is to design, manufacture, and deliver products that meet and exceed the needs and expectations of each customer.", "founded_year": "1990", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='tz-medical-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Tabor Plastics Company was founded in 1955 by plastics pioneer Carl Tabor in St. Louis, Missouri. The business remains family-run, guided by the founder''s original dedication to cutting-edge injection molding processes, customer care, expert problem-solving, and community investment.

The company operates as a full-service custom precision injection molder, offering overmolding, insert molding, mold design optimization, mold maintenance and adjustments, new tooling capabilities (domestic or foreign), packaging, and comprehensive post-molding services. Its facility is continuously updated with the latest equipment and a wide inventory of engineering-grade thermoplastics, though headcount and plant size are not publicly disclosed.

Tabor serves original equipment manufacturers across demanding sectors, including lighting, refrigeration, valves and custom valve fixtures, furniture, shipping fixtures, and handheld fixtures. The company emphasizes its role as a go-to partner for OEMs that require consistent quality and on-time delivery.

Founding values extend beyond the shop floor: Tabor established and sustains the Carl J. Tabor Scholarship at Pittsburg State University and supports St. Louis food banks and women''s shelters. Leadership describes the firm as an old-fashioned company more concerned with excellence than profits, backing that stance with guaranteed tolerances of ±0.001 inch and a commitment to deliver parts when customers need them.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom precision injection molding", "Overmolding", "Insert molding", "Mold design optimization", "Mold maintenance and adjustments", "New tooling capabilities (domestic or foreign)", "Packaging services", "Post-molding services"], "industries": ["Lighting", "Refrigeration", "Valves and custom valve fixtures", "Furniture", "Shipping fixtures", "Handheld fixtures"], "materials": ["ABS (Acrylonitrile Butadiene Styrene)", "HDPE (High-Density Polyethylene)", "LDPE (Low-Density Polyethylene)", "HIPS (High Impact Polystyrene)", "PET (Polyethylene Terephthalate)", "PP (Polypropylene)", "POM (Polyacetal)", "PPS (Polyphenylene sulfide)", "PA 6 & PA 6/6 (Polyamide)", "PC (Polycarbonate)", "TPU (Thermoplastic Polyurethane)"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "\u00b10.001 in", "built_on": ["Guaranteed tolerances of \u00b10.001 inch", "Guaranteed on-time delivery", "In-house mold optimization and post-molding services", "Wide inventory of engineering-grade thermoplastics", "Family-owned, focused on excellence over profits"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1955 by Carl Tabor -> /", "Family-run ownership -> /", "Headquarters St. Louis, Missouri -> db", "Custom precision injection molding, overmolding, insert molding -> /services", "Mold design optimization, mold maintenance, new tooling, packaging, post-molding services -> /", "Guaranteed tolerances of .001'''' -> /about", "Materials: ABS, HDPE, LDPE, HIPS, PET, PP, POM, PPS, PA 6/6, PC, TPU -> /services", "Industries: lighting, refrigeration, valves/custom valve fixtures, furniture, shipping fixtures, handheld fixtures -> / and /services", "Carl J. Tabor Scholarship at Pittsburg State University, donations to food banks and women''s shelters -> /", "70 years of success, latest equipment, wide material inventory -> /", "In-house mold optimization and post-molding services -> /services", "Guaranteed on-time delivery -> /about", "Old-fashioned company more concerned with excellence than profits -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Tabor Plastics is an elite plastic injection molding manufacturer who takes pride in exceptional craftsmanship and our uncompromising customer service.", "founded_year": "1955", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='tabor-plastics-company' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Tactical Electric operates as Tactical Contractors Inc. from its base in New York City, serving all five boroughs with a focus on Downtown Manhattan neighborhoods such as the Financial District, Tribeca, SoHo, Chelsea, and the West Village. The company does not disclose a founding year or founder names in its public materials, describing its tenure only as "a long time" and emphasizing years of experience among its licensed electricians.

The firm provides residential and commercial electrical contracting services, including full rewiring, panel upgrades and repairs, sub-panel installations, lighting design and installation (recessed, track, accent, bathroom, kitchen, dimming systems), troubleshooting, safety inspections, dedicated circuitry for home offices, and outlet installation. It offers 24/7 emergency response and same-day service for urgent issues. No facility size, headcount, or project volume figures are published.

Customers range from apartment and brownstone owners in historic districts to commercial tenants in Midtown and the Financial District. The company works with general contractors on pre-renovation inspections and punch lists, and serves property managers handling lease turnovers. Specific neighborhoods cited include Gramercy, Flatiron, Nolita, the Upper East and West Sides, Battery Park, and the Lower East Side.

Tactical Electric positions itself on professionalism, reliability, and affordability, highlighting clear communication, upfront pricing, and a policy of returning to complete repairs free of charge if an issue is not resolved on the first visit. Its electricians are licensed and insured, and the company stresses safety-first practices such as whole-house surge protection, GFCI and AFCI compliance, and childproof outlets.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Residential electrical wiring and rewiring", "Commercial electrical contracting", "Electrical panel upgrades and repairs", "Sub-panel installation", "Recessed lighting installation", "Track and accent lighting installation", "Bathroom and kitchen lighting installation", "Lighting dimmer and timer installation", "Electrical troubleshooting and diagnostics", "Electrical safety inspections (load testing, GFCI/AFCI checks)", "Dedicated computer circuitry installation", "Circuit breaker replacement", "Outlet installation (USB, tamper-resistant, GFCI)", "Whole-house surge protector installation", "Emergency electrical repairs (24/7)", "Lighting design and layout"], "industries": ["Residential", "Commercial", "Construction", "Property Management", "Real Estate"], "materials": ["Electrical wiring and cable", "Circuit breakers and panels", "Lighting fixtures and controls", "Outlets and receptacles (GFCI, USB, tamper-resistant)", "Surge protection devices", "Dimming system components", "Recessed lighting cans and trims", "Track lighting heads and rails"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "Same-day service available; 24/7 emergency response", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Same-day service available", "24/7 emergency electrical response", "Licensed and insured electricians on every job", "Free return visits if repairs not resolved on first attempt", "Upfront pricing with no hidden fees"], "facts_used": ["Company name Tactical Electric and Tactical Contractors Inc -> /", "Headquarters New York City, serves all five boroughs -> /", "Services: residential and commercial electrical contracting, rewiring, panel upgrades, sub-panels, lighting installation, troubleshooting, safety inspections, dedicated circuitry, outlet installation -> /", "24/7 emergency service and same-day service -> /", "Licensed and insured electricians -> /", "Free return visits if not fixed first time -> /", "Upfront pricing, clear communication -> /", "Neighborhoods served: Financial District, Tribeca, SoHo, Chelsea, West Village, Gramercy, Flatiron, Nolita, Upper East Side, Upper West Side, Battery Park, Lower East Side, Midtown -> /", "Customer types: residential owners, commercial tenants, general contractors, property managers -> /", "Safety practices: whole-house surge protection, GFCI/AFCI compliance, childproof outlets -> /"], "company_type": "Installer / service company", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "Our licensed residential electricians put safety and quality first\u2014handling everything from lighting upgrades and dimming systems to full rewires and emergency repairs.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='tactical-electric' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Taliaferro Imports, Inc., doing business as GenuineSaab.com, is a family-owned and operated company based in Springfield, Missouri. Established in 1990, the business has remained in the same building since its founding.

The company operates a CNC machine shop with four CNC machines, producing its own line of Saab performance parts that are used globally on high-performance Saab vehicles. In addition to manufacturing, Taliaferro Imports offers in-house chassis dynamometer services for customer rental, product development, and validation, supported by advanced data acquisition capabilities. The firm also stocks and distributes factory Saab parts, aftermarket Swedish performance components, and provides ECU calibration services. Orders are shipped worldwide via UPS.

Taliaferro Imports serves Saab owners, enthusiasts, and repair shops worldwide. Its customer base includes individuals seeking genuine Saab parts and performance upgrades, as well as professional tuners utilizing the company’s dyno and development services. The company is an authorized BSR performance dealer, and its manufactured parts are noted as being used on some of the world’s fastest Saabs.

The company emphasizes its identity as “Genuine Saab People” who use the parts they sell, highlighting knowledgeable, prompt, and enthusiastic service. Its in-house manufacturing and dyno capabilities allow for product validation and custom parts development, differentiating it from pure resellers.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["CNC machining", "Chassis dynamometer testing", "Product development and validation", "Advanced data acquisition", "Custom parts manufacturing", "Saab parts distribution", "Aftermarket performance parts distribution", "ECU calibration", "Service bulletin and installation documentation"], "industries": ["Automotive aftermarket", "Saab performance parts", "Automotive performance tuning"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["CNC machines (4)", "Chassis dynamometer"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Family owned and operated from the same location since 1990", "In-house CNC manufacturing of performance parts used on world\u2019s fastest Saabs", "On-site chassis dynamometer for product development, validation, and customer rental", "Authorized BSR performance dealer", "Worldwide shipping via UPS with computerized tracking"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1990, family-owned, same building -> /", "CNC machine shop with 4 CNC machines -> /", "In-house chassis dyno for product development/validation -> /", "Authorized BSR performance dealer -> /", "Worldwide shipping via UPS -> /", "Manufactures own performance parts -> /", "Distributes factory Saab parts and aftermarket Swedish performance parts -> /", "Instagram link -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "our own performance parts manufactured in house that are used worldwide on some of the worlds fastest Saabs", "founded_year": "1990", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": ["https://instagram.com/genuinesaab/"], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='taliaferro-imports' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Tall T, doing business as TallT, is an apparel brand headquartered in Denver, Colorado. The company does not publicly disclose its founding year, ownership structure, or the names of its founders.

TallT designs and sells a range of snow sports and streetwear products, including the TallT x MaxReade Snowpants V3, Classic Logo hoodies, graphic t-shirts such as the Ichwawa and Blank Tee, headwear like the Boonie Hat and Snapback, face masks, and accessory packs. Products are offered through a direct-to-consumer e-commerce site and a wholesale channel for retail partners. The company also operates a mobile shopping application.

Product lines feature extended sizing options, including tall fits labeled XL TALL, 3XL TALL, and 5XL TALL.

TallT states that its mission is to provide confidence on the mountain, emphasizing that its pants are designed to deliver a feeling of performance and style rather than simply a product.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Apparel design", "Wholesale distribution", "E-commerce retail", "Athlete collaboration", "Mobile commerce"], "industries": ["Snow sports", "Outdoor recreation", "Streetwear", "Apparel retail", "Wholesale"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": [], "facts_used": ["Headquarters: Denver, Colorado -> db", "Product categories: Shirts, Outerwear, Face Masks, Headwear, Accessories -> /", "Collaborations with Henrik Harlaut and Max Reade -> /", "Wholesale channel -> /", "Mobile app -> /", "Extended tall sizing options -> /", "Mission statement about confidence on the mountain -> db", "Copyright 2026 -> /", "Social media icons: Facebook, Twitter, Instagram, Vimeo -> /"], "company_type": "Retailer", "makes_products": "unclear", "type_evidence": "The website features a consumer-facing shop with categories including Shirts, Outerwear, Face Masks, Headwear, and Accessories, plus a Wholesale link for business customers.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='tall-t' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Tampa Clothing Company operates from Hudson, Florida, as a family-owned custom apparel manufacturer. The company produces all-over dye-sublimated garments entirely in the United States and does not outsource any production steps.

The shop focuses on full-color dye sublimation across a catalog of shirts, polos, hoodies, tanks, and fleece items in sizes from youth small to 8X. Design turnaround is quoted at seven days, with production shipping two to three weeks after artwork approval. No minimum order quantities are required, and the company handles design, manufacturing, and fulfillment in-house.

Customers span business and brand launches, event and promotional needs, corporate uniform programs, sports teams requiring jerseys with names and numbers, trades and services such as pressure washing and property maintenance, and schools or groups ordering personalized class and club apparel.

