UPDATE companies SET description='Taylor Sales and Service operates from Birmingham, Alabama, as a locally owned and operated distributor of foodservice equipment and products. The company has served the state for over three decades, with leadership including President Jimmy Palmer and Sales Manager James Palmer.

Its capabilities include preventive maintenance, emergency repair, new-equipment installation, parts supply, and a state-of-the-art test kitchen where customers can trial the latest Taylor models. A team of Taylor-certified technicians, a dedicated parts manager, and an install crew support operations across Alabama.

Customers range from independent restaurants and frozen-yogurt shops to national quick-service chains such as McDonald’s and Chick-fil-A, as well as convenience stores and institutional accounts like the University of Alabama at Birmingham. Technicians are frequently dispatched to service ice cream machines, frozen cocktail dispensers, custard freezers, and grills at these locations.

The company emphasizes a value system built on integrity, persistence, knowledge, teamwork, passion, and work-life balance. It highlights “master level know-how” from its certified technicians and notes that one of its technicians, Allen Hinkle, earned the Red Cape Technician of the Year award in 2022.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Foodservice equipment sales", "Equipment installation", "Preventive maintenance", "Emergency repair service", "Parts supply and management", "Test kitchen demonstrations", "Taylor-brand equipment specialization", "Dispatch and service coordination"], "industries": ["Foodservice", "Restaurants", "Quick-service restaurants", "Frozen yogurt shops", "Convenience stores", "Institutional foodservice"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["Taylor foodservice equipment", "Test kitchen equipment"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Taylor-certified technicians with master-level expertise", "State-of-the-art test kitchen for equipment trials", "Dedicated parts, installation, and dispatch teams", "Red Cape Technician of the Year 2022 recognition"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters in Birmingham, Alabama -> db", "Locally owned and operated distributor of foodservice equipment and products -> /about-us", "Serving Alabama for over 32 years (40 years on homepage) -> /, /about-us", "Leadership: Jimmy Palmer (President), James Palmer (Sales Manager), Allen Scales (Service Manager), Rob Bright (Territory Manager \u2013 North AL), Patrick Taylor (Territory Manager \u2013 South AL), April Fields (Dispatch), Helen Bullock (Service Coordinator), Heath Stockton (Parts Manager), Brandon Moore (Install Team) -> /about-us", "Services: equipment sales, installation, preventive maintenance, emergency repair, parts supply, test kitchen demonstrations -> /, /about-us", "Taylor-certified technicians mentioned -> /", "Test kitchen with latest Taylor equipment -> /", "Industries served: restaurants, fast food (McDonald''s, Chick-fil-A), frozen yogurt shops (Cold Snap), convenience stores (Liberty Convenience Center), institutional (UAB) -> /", "Technicians named in reviews: Scooter, Terry, Phil, Jimmy, Michael, Masaki, Kavin, Jesse, Allen Hinkle -> /", "Values: Integrity, Persistence, Knowledge, Team, PASSIONATE, Balanced -> /, /about-us", "Red Cape Technician of the Year 2022: Allen Hinkle -> /"], "company_type": "Distributor / reseller", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "Taylor Sales and Service is a specialized foodservice equipment and product distributor.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='taylor-sales-and-service' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Team 1 Plastics operates from Albion, Michigan, a central Midwestern location that the company says allows easy access for customer molding trials and technical meetings. The founding year and ownership structure are not disclosed in public materials, and no founders are named.

The company specializes in precision and transparent plastic injection molding for the transportation sector. Its facility runs 24/7 with a highly automated line: every press is equipped with robots to reduce handling damage and labor costs. Team 1 Plastics emphasizes low mold cavitation — very few tools exceed eight cavities — which it says delivers higher precision and repeatable quality matched to each customer’s annual volume. Beyond molding, it provides value‑added assembly, part consolidation, supply‑chain services (returnable packaging, custom labeling, bar‑code tracking, day/night shipments via its own fleet or customer milk runs), and manages new tool design or transfer tooling bring‑up.

Customers include automotive OEMs and Tier suppliers, as well as manufacturers of oil, fuel (gasoline and diesel), and air filtration systems. The company’s components appear in automobile systems and filtration products across these segments.

Team 1 Plastics states its differentiation rests on a disciplined quality system certified to IATF 16949:2016 and ISO 9001:2015, a zero‑defect mentality supported by cross‑functional corrective‑action meetings, and an Activity‑Based Costing model updated through self‑evaluation and customer feedback.', certifications=ARRAY['IATF 16949:2016','ISO 9001:2015','ISO/TS 16949:2009']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Plastic injection molding", "Precision molding", "Transparent/clear plastic molding", "Value\u2011added assembly", "Part consolidation", "Supply chain management", "Returnable packaging", "Custom labeling", "Bar\u2011code scanning and tracking", "Tool design and construction management", "Transfer tooling integration", "New product launch management", "Activity\u2011Based Costing quoting", "Capacity planning and inventory management"], "industries": ["Transportation", "Automotive", "Oil and gas filtration", "Fuel filtration (gasoline and diesel)", "Air filtration"], "materials": ["Thermoplastics", "Resins"], "equipment": ["Injection molding presses with robots", "Small molding machines", "Bar\u2011code scanning equipment"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["24/7 production and logistics operation", "Every injection molding press equipped with robots", "Low mold cavitation (max 8 cavities) for higher precision", "No rush\u2011order or schedule\u2011break fees for unplanned orders", "Activity\u2011Based Costing model for quote accuracy", "Own fleet for day/night shipments and milk\u2011run delivery", "Weekly cross\u2011functional new product launch meetings"], "facts_used": ["Location: Albion, Michigan -> db (hq_city, hq_state_label) and home page", "Plastic injection molding for transportation industry -> db (description)", "Specializes in precision and clear plastic components -> db (description)", "24/7 production and logistics operation -> home page", "Every press equipped with robots -> home page", "Low mold cavitation (max 8 cavities) -> quality page", "IATF 16949:2016 certified -> quality page", "ISO 9001:2015 certified -> quality page", "ISO/TS 16949:2009 certified since 2013 -> quality page", "Value\u2011added assembly and part consolidation -> home page", "Supply chain solutions: returnable packaging, custom labeling, bar\u2011code tracking, own fleet -> home page", "No rush\u2011order fees for drop\u2011in orders -> home page", "Activity\u2011Based Costing model -> home page", "Weekly cross\u2011functional new product launch meetings -> home page and quality page", "Serves automotive, oil/fuel filtration, air filtration -> home page (Products & Systems section)", "Manages tool design/construction and transfer tooling -> quality page", "Reduction >50% external rejects 2015\u20112018 -> quality page", "Global network of partner vendors -> home page", "Centrally located in Midwest for customer access -> home page"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "As a plastic injection molding company for the transportation industry, Team 1 Plastics specializes in precision and clear plastic components", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='team-1-plastics' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Team Technologies is based in Albuquerque, New Mexico, operating from a 36,000-square-foot facility that houses engineering, machining, and electronics assembly under one roof. The founding year and ownership structure are not publicly disclosed.

The company provides new product design, development, and supplemental engineering services alongside manufacturing capabilities. Its machine shop runs CNC vertical milling (3-, 4-, and 5-axis), CNC tool room lathes with live tooling, wire and sinker EDM (wire down to 0.001 inch), surface grinding, and precision welding (TIG, MIG, and Class 4 laser). The electronics side offers full turnkey PCB and box-build assembly, SMT and through-hole placement with dual automated pick-and-place lines handling 0201 components and BGAs, 2D X-ray and AOI inspection, in-circuit test, custom cable assembly, and sub-assembly fabrication. Metrology includes two DCC CMMs (750 × 750 × 550 mm), a DCC optical video gauge, and surface plates.

Team Technologies serves government and commercial clients, with noted work in aerospace components, biomedical devices, RF products, and video/data systems. The company also supports energetic materials such as firesets and CDUs, and provides obsolescence lifecycle management.

