UPDATE companies SET description='Technical Services Inc (TSI) operates from a 100,000-square-foot facility in Oak Harbor, Washington. The company is employee-owned, meaning the workforce holds a direct stake in the business.

TSI provides electronics manufacturing services including surface-mount and through-hole PCB assembly, box builds, X-ray inspection, and turnkey procurement. The plant runs six SMT lines capable of high-mix to high-volume production, and offers conformal coating in acrylic and polyurethane, functional/ICT/RF testing with partner-developed fixtures, programming, labeling, and complete box-build integration. The company supports fast ramp from new product introduction to production with flexible volumes and offers DFM/DFX support along with turnkey, consignment, or hybrid material strategies.

The company serves aerospace and military, commercial, medical, and industrial markets. For aerospace and military customers it builds mission-critical electronics to IPC Class 3 with full component traceability. Medical clients receive quality-sensitive builds with documented controls and ISO 13485 certification. Industrial customers get rugged control and power electronics designed for uptime, while commercial programs benefit from rapid NPI-to-production scaling and cost-down supply chain options.

TSI emphasizes its employee-ownership model as a differentiator, stating that every build is personal because the team owns the outcome. It cites a 99.96% on-time delivery rate over a rolling 12-month period, an RMA rate below 0.6%, and a certified quality system encompassing ISO 9001, AS9100D, and ISO 13485. The company also highlights Class 3 workmanship with 100% automated optical inspection on both sides of assemblies and full supply chain management from PCBAs to complete box builds.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001','AS9100D','ISO 13485']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Conformal coating (acrylic & polyurethane) for rugged environments", "Serialization and component-level traceability from incoming to shipment", "Fast ramp from NPI to production with flexible volumes", "DFM/DFX support and cost-down supply chain options", "Programming, labeling, and complete box-build", "Turnkey, consignment, or hybrid material strategies", "Class 3 workmanship and full component traceability", "Functional/ICT/RF test with partner-developed fixtures", "PCBA Assembly (SMT & Through-Hole)", "Box Builds", "X-ray Inspection", "Turnkey Procurement Solutions"], "industries": ["Aerospace / Military", "Commercial", "Medical", "Industrial"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["Six SMT lines", "Automated optical inspection (AOI)", "X-ray inspection system"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Employee-owned structure aligning workforce incentives with customer outcomes", "100,000 sq ft facility with six modern SMT lines", "99.96% on-time delivery (rolling 12 months)", "RMA rate under 0.6% over the last year", "Certified to ISO 9001, AS9100D, and ISO 13485"], "facts_used": ["Company name and location -> db", "Employee-owned ownership -> /", "100,000 sq ft facility with six SMT lines -> /", "Certifications: ISO 9001, AS9100D, ISO 13485 -> /", "Capabilities: PCBA assembly, box builds, X-ray inspection, turnkey procurement, conformal coating, functional/ICT/RF t