UPDATE companies SET description='Tenneco Inc is headquartered in Marshall, Michigan, and traces its roots back over a century in the transportation industry. The company operates under the leadership of CEO Jim Voss, though the INPUT does not specify its founding year, ownership structure, or original founders.

The company designs, engineers, and manufactures clean air, powertrain, and ride performance systems through four business segments: Clean Air, Powertrain, Performance Solutions, and DRiV. Its global footprint spans 169 manufacturing sites, 39 engineering and technical facilities, and 28 countries, supported by approximately 58,000 team members. The DRiV segment alone encompasses more than 30 aftermarket brands.

Tenneco serves original equipment manufacturers across light vehicle, commercial truck, and off-highway vehicle markets, as well as the automotive aftermarket through its DRiV portfolio. Its technologies address emissions control, fuel economy, acoustic performance, safety, and comfort for customers worldwide.

Its operating values emphasize radical candor, simplification, organizational velocity, tenacious execution, and winning. Sustainability targets include a 33 percent reduction in recordable incident rates, an 18 percent cut in energy consumption, and 75 percent waste recycling across manufacturing operations, with 90 percent of sites certified to ISO 14001.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 14001 Environmental Management System']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Emissions control system design", "Emissions control system engineering", "Emissions control system manufacturing", "Engine component design", "Engine component engineering", "Engine component manufacturing", "Ride performance system design", "Ride performance system engineering", "Ride performance system manufacturing", "Aftermarket parts manufacturing", "Aftermarket parts distribution", "Clean air solutions development", "Powertrain solutions development", "Performance solutions development"], "industries": ["Transportation", "Automotive OEM", "Commercial vehicle", "Off-highway vehicle", "Automotive aftermarket"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["58,000 global team members across 169 manufacturing sites", "39 engineering and technical facilities in 28 countries", "90% of manufacturing sites certified to ISO 14001", "More than 30 aftermarket brands under DRiV", "Four integrated business segments: Clean Air, Powertrain, Performance Solutions, DRiV"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters in Marshall, Michigan -> db", "58,000 global team members -> /", "169 manufacturing sites -> /", "39 engineering and technical facilities -> /", "28 countries -> /", "CEO Jim Voss -> /about-us", "Four business segments: Clean Air, Powertrain, Performance Solutions, DRiV -> /", "More than 30 aftermarket brands under DRiV -> /", "Serves light vehicle, commercial truck, off-highway vehicle OEMs -> /", "Serves automotive aftermarket -> /", "90% of manufacturing sites certified to ISO 14001 -> /", "Sustainability metrics: 33% reduction in recordable incident rate, 18% reduction in energy consumption, 75% waste recycled -> /about-us", "Company purpose: most trusted partner and best manufacturer/distributor in transportation industry -> /, /about-us", "Values: Radical Candor, Simplify, Organizational velocity, Tenacious execution, Win -> /about-us"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "We build what vehicles cannot run without \u2014 clean air, powertrain, and ride performance systems engineered to perform under real-world pressure.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "58,000", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='tenneco-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Tennessee Metal Fabricating, now operating as a Victaulic brand, is based in Rock Island, Tennessee. In September 2022, Victaulic, a manufacturer of mechanical pipe joining solutions, acquired the business assets of TMF and welcomed its employees into the Victaulic family. The original founding year and ownership structure of TMF are not disclosed in the available information.

The facility comprises three buildings totaling 125,000 square feet. Shop equipment includes plate rollers, automatic submerged arc welding machines, manual MIG and TIG welding machines, and Victaulic roll groove equipment. The paint shop applies epoxy coatings in accordance with AWWA standards. The company fabricates pipe up to 144 inches in diameter with 3/4-inch wall thickness in carbon and stainless steel. Special testing capabilities include hydrostatic, X-ray, ultrasonic, and magnetic particle inspection. Products are manufactured to AWWA standards such as C200, C205, C207, C208, C209, C210, and C222.

The company serves waterworks and infrastructure projects, producing steel water pipe and fittings for municipal and industrial piping systems.

