UPDATE companies SET description='Tezzaron Semiconductor Corporation is headquartered in Naperville, Illinois. The company entered the spotlight in 2004 when it demonstrated the world''s first successful wafer-stacked 3D integrated circuits with through-silicon interconnects, including microprocessors, sensors, and SRAM devices. While the exact founding year and ownership structure are not publicly disclosed, the firm has since collaborated with dozens of customers to develop custom 3D-ICs for both prototyping and commercial production.

Tezzaron''s core offering is its Di3D technology, a transistor-level 3D integration platform that combines wafer bonding, proprietary SuperContacts®, dis-integrated architectures, and BiSTAR® programmable self-test. The company handles the full development flow: adapting design tools, rewriting floor-planning rules, inventing and fabricating new structures, and creating novel test techniques and circuits. This end-to-end capability enables high-density, high-speed vertical interconnects in a footprint the size of a single die.

The technology targets high-performance semiconductor applications, including microprocessors, sensors, and memory devices. Tezzaron has participated in multiple multi-project wafer (MPW) runs for 3D-IC prototypes, partnering with organizations such as CMP (Circuits Multi Projets) in France. Its customer base spans companies seeking custom 3D-IC solutions for prototyping and volume commercialization.

The company states that its approach "changes everything" about 3D integration, aiming to build a Di3D™ ecosystem of partners and licensees where the high-performance world can raise the bar for density and speed.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Wafer bonding", "3D-IC design and floor-planning", "Custom 3D-IC prototyping", "Multi-project wafer (MPW) participation", "BiSTAR\u00ae programmable self-test implementation", "SuperContacts\u00ae fabrication", "Dis-integrated architecture development", "Through-silicon interconnect fabrication", "Design tool adaptation for 3D integration", "Test technique and circuit development"], "industries": ["Semiconductor", "High-performance computing", "Microprocessors", "Sensors", "Memory (SRAM)", "3D integration"], "materials": ["Silicon wafers"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["TSV-free 3D stacking achieving single-die footprint", "Proprietary SuperContacts\u00ae for vertical interconnect", "BiSTAR\u00ae programmable self-test enabling post-assembly repair", "Dis-integrated architecture design methodology", "Di3D\u2122 ecosystem of partners and licensees"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters in Naperville, Illinois -> db", "2004 demonstration of world''s first wafer-stacked 3D-ICs with through-silicon interconnect -> /", "Worked with dozens of customers to create custom 3D-ICs for prototyping and commercialization -> /", "Di3D technology uses wafer bonding, SuperContacts\u00ae, dis-integrated architectures, BiSTAR\u00ae self-test -> /", "Full development flow: design tool adaptation, floor-planning rewrite, new structure invention/fabrication/verification, new test techniques/circuits -> /about-us", "Participated in multiple MPWs for 3D-IC prototypes, partner CMP in France -> /about", "Target applications: microprocessors, sensors, SRAM devices -> /", "Goal: build Di3D\u2122 ecosystem of partners and licensees -> /about-us", "TSV-free 3D: stacks size of a sing