UPDATE companies SET description='The Kitchen Guys LLC is headquartered in Slidell, Louisiana, and traces its roots to 1955 when Hoyt Refrigeration Co. began manufacturing and installing convenience-store and supermarket equipment in Lecompte, Louisiana. The firm remains family-owned and operates from its Slidell base while serving clients nationwide.

The company provides end-to-end commercial kitchen services: consulting and design, equipment procurement through two major buying groups, project coordination and logistics, custom equipment specification with shop drawings, installation using local and national crews, and ongoing service and leasing (including dishmachine leasing). They handle projects ranging from single-equipment replacements to large-scale stadium and hotel kitchens, and they produce rough-in coordination drawings for general contractors.

Their customer base spans restaurants, hotels, schools, stadiums, supermarkets, convenience stores, and multi-unit chain concepts across the continental United States. The team includes professionals who have worked inside restaurants, not just designed for them, which informs their practical approach to workflow and code compliance.

The Kitchen Guys differentiate themselves through unlimited design revisions until the client approves the final layout, a core-values framework they call “The Kitchen Guys’ Way” (committed, persistent, innovative, fun), and a promise to manage all logistics and storage in sync with construction schedules so that damaged or delayed items are communicated immediately.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Kitchen consulting and design", "Equipment procurement", "Installation management", "Custom equipment specification", "Foodservice equipment service and repair", "Dishmachine leasing", "Project coordination and logistics", "Rough-in coordination drawings", "Shop drawings for custom fabrication"], "industries": ["Restaurants", "Hotels", "Schools", "Stadiums", "Supermarkets", "Convenience stores", "Chain restaurants"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Unlimited design revisions until client sign-off", "Staff with hands-on restaurant experience", "Membership in two major equipment buying groups", "National installation network with specialized refrigeration and beer-system technicians", "Project logistics coordinated to construction schedule"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters in Slidell, Louisiana -> db", "Founded 2022 as The Kitchen Guys -> /about-us", "Lineage from Hoyt Refrigeration Co. (1955) -> /about-us", "Family-owned, three generations -> /about-us", "Services: consulting, design, procurement, installation, custom equipment, service & leasing -> /services", "Two major buying groups membership -> /services", "Local and national installation crews -> /services", "Unlimited design revisions -> /about-us", "Core values: The Kitchen Guys'' Way -> /about-us", "Industries: restaurants, hotels, schools, stadiums, supermarkets, c-stores, chains -> /about-us, /services", "Project scale: replacement to stadium projects -> /about-us", "Nationwide service (continental U.S.) -> /services", "Rough-in coordination drawings -> /services", "Shop drawings for custom fabrication -> /services", "Dishmachine leasing -> /services"], "company_type": "Installer / service company", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "Commercial Kitchen Equipment and Design Firm based in New Orleans, Louisiana.", "founded_year": "2022", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='the-kitchen-guys-llc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='The business launched in June 2012 when chef Mark LaCasse and his wife Kelly returned to central Maine after years of culinary and hospitality work across the U.S. and abroad. Mark, a 2007 graduate of the Culinary Institute of America, represents the third generation of his family to run a business from the property; their two sons are the fifth generation to grow up in Skowhegan.

The company produces a line of gourmet prepared frozen meals designed for boil-in-bag convenience, ready in 20 minutes or less. Recipes draw on classic culinary techniques and feature ingredients sourced from Maine farms and coastal waters—beef, chicken, seafood, vegetables, herbs, artisan pasta, honey, maple syrup, whole grains, dairy, and handcrafted cheeses. Production takes place in a commercial kitchen licensed by the Maine Department of Agriculture and the USDA as a food manufacturer. The facility also houses a retail shop and a seasonal popsicle window, serving walk-in customers and pre-order pickups.

The Maine Meal sells directly to consumers through home delivery (doorstep and dockside to boats, campgrounds, and businesses), farmers markets, and its retail store. Wholesale accounts include specialty food shops, grocery stores, restaurants, farm stands, tasting rooms, campgrounds, ocean and lake marinas, and Maine schools. A new provisioning service targets long-haul vessels traveling the Maine coast.

The founders frame the business as a vehicle to strengthen the regional food system. By purchasing from local farmers and fishermen, they aim to create sustainable sales channels for Maine producers. The company emphasizes sustainably grown, harvested, and foraged ingredients, and positions its meals as a way to simplify mealtime without sacrificing nutritional quality or culinary tradition.', certifications=ARRAY['Maine Department of Agriculture food manufacturer license','USDA food manufacturer license']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Prepared frozen meal manufacturing", "Boil-in-bag meal production", "Food gift packaging", "Wholesale distribution to retail and foodservice", "Direct-to-consumer frozen meal delivery", "Farmers market vending", "Retail shop operation", "Commercial kitchen production", "Vessel provisioning service"], "industries": ["Specialty food retail", "Grocery stores", "Restaurants", "Farm stands", "Tasting rooms", "Campgrounds", "Marinas", "School food service", "Direct-to-consumer meal delivery", "Farmers markets"], "materials": ["Maine beef", "Maine chicken", "Maine seafood", "Maine vegetables", "Maine herbs", "Artisan pasta", "Honey", "Maple syrup", "Whole grains", "Milk", "Cream", "Handcrafted cheeses", "Eggs", "Fruits", "Dairy"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Meals ready in 20 minutes via boil-in-bag preparation", "Ingredients sourced exclusively from Maine farms and coastal waters", "Licensed by Maine Department of Agriculture and USDA as a food manufacturer", "Family-owned operation in a third-generation building on the Kennebec River", "Provisioning service for long-haul vessels along the Maine coast"], "facts_used": ["Founded June 2012 -> /about-us", "Family-owned, third generation building -> /about-us", "Licensed by Maine Dept of Agriculture and USDA -> /about-us", "Commercial kitchen, retail shop, popsicle window at 4 Madison Ave -> /", "Wholesale to specialty shops, grocery stores, restaurants, etc. -> /", "Delivery and pickup services -> /", "Ingredients from Maine farms and coastal waters -> /", "Provision service for long-haul vessels -> /", "Mark LaCasse CIA graduate 2007 -> /about-us", "Kelly LaCasse co-owner -> /about-us", "Located in Skowhegan, Maine -> /", "No shipping currently -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "The Maine Meal is a small, family run business licensed through the Maine Department of Agriculture and the USDA as a food manufacturer.", "founded_year": "2012", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned", "Small business"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='the-maine-meal' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='The Olive Oil Factory Store operates a family-owned and operated tasting room in Waterbury, Connecticut. The business sells gourmet olive oils, vinegars, and specialty foods both in-store and online through its Delavignes brand.

The store offers a rotating selection of extra virgin olive oils, balsamic and golden balsamic vinegars, gift baskets, and pantry items such as cheesemaking kits, baking extracts, and heirloom popcorn. Every Friday the kitchen produces traditional focaccia breads and sourdough baguettes for immediate sale. The retail space is open Monday through Friday 9 a.m. to 5 p.m. and Saturday 10 a.m. to 3 p.m., with free samples available for visitors.

The company sources local artisan cheeses and charcuterie from producers in Litchfield and New Haven Counties, and carries imported products such as Spanish organic extra virgin olive oil and authentic Prosciutto di Parma.

