UPDATE companies SET description='The Peterson Company operates from Auburn, Washington, with a second production facility in Moonachie, New Jersey. The business, also known as Peterson Foods, has built a reputation as a specialty food supplier and value-added processor for the Pacific Northwest and beyond. No founding year or ownership details are publicly stated.

The company maintains a broad catalog of domestic and imported artisan cheeses, charcuterie, bakery items, and specialty ingredients, available through a 24/7 online ordering system. Its core manufacturing service is custom cutting and packing: two third-party-audited facilities provide hand wrapping, shrink wrapping, cryovac vacuum packaging, cheese cubing, portioning into cups or bags, variety tray and gift box assembly, and custom labeling. The same lines also handle chocolate, candies, and nuts.

Buyers cite the one-stop-shop inventory, free delivery, and responsive customer service as reasons they consolidate purchasing through the company.

Peterson positions its cutting and packing service as a way for clients to eliminate in-house labor, trim loss, and liability while preserving freshness and upscale presentation. The monthly Provisions Flyer highlights seasonal items across cheese, charcuterie, bakery, and ingredient categories.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Hand wrapping for soft and hard cheeses", "Single or double shrink wrap", "Cryovac vacuum packaging", "Cheese cubing", "Custom packaging", "Portioning in cups, bags", "Variety trays and gift box assembly", "Custom labeling and pre-pricing"], "industries": ["Foodservice", "Restaurant", "Retail", "Specialty food", "Hospitality"], "materials": ["Cheese (soft and hard)", "Chocolate", "Candies", "Nuts"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["24/7 online ordering with real-time pricing", "Free delivery on orders", "Third-party-audited production facilities in two locations", "Custom cutting, packing, and labeling for cheese, chocolate, nuts", "Monthly Provisions Flyer for seasonal product updates"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters in Auburn, WA -> db", "Second facility in Moonachie, NJ -> /services", "24/7 online ordering catalog -> /", "Cutting and packing services: hand wrapping, shrink wrap, cryovac, cubing, portioning, variety trays, gift boxes, custom labeling -> /services", "Works with cheese, chocolate, candies, nuts -> /services", "Third-party-audited facilities -> /services", "Customer testimonial: 25-year relationship with pastry chef at Ray''s Boathouse -> /", "Customer testimonial: one-stop shop, free delivery, stellar service -> /", "Monthly Provisions Flyer for seasonal items -> /", "LinkedIn URL -> db"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Our fully equipped, 3rd party-audited production facilities in Auburn, WA and Moonachie, NJ offer unique packaging solutions and custom cut sizes to meet a wide range of business needs.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": ["https://www.linkedin.com/company/peterson-cheese/"], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='the-peterson-company' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='The Sam Tell Companies traces its roots to 1956, when Sam Tell and his son Neil opened a two-person operation on Bleecker Street in New York City. The family-owned dealership began with a focus on dependable foodservice solutions, and by the 1980s the founder''s grandson Marc Tell had joined the business alongside Dan Saltzman. Today Marc serves as chief executive, a team of 180 from two Long Island warehouses and a Manhattan design showroom.

The company operates as a full-service foodservice equipment and supplies dealer, offering design, build, and supply capabilities under one roof. Its award-winning design team creates commercial kitchen layouts, while skilled installers handle equipment placement and project execution. The supply division stocks tens of thousands of products ranging from smallwares to heavy equipment, and the firm provides shipping and delivery across the tri-state area and nationwide. Sam Tell ranks as the 30th largest foodservice equipment and supplies distributor in the United States.

Clients span restaurants and bars, sports and entertainment venues, hospitality, corporate dining, healthcare, education, country clubs, retail, and airport and travel lounges. Notable projects include the kitchen at Lure Fishbar, where chef Josh Capon credited Sam Tell with building the "heart and soul" of the operation.

The company emphasizes what it calls the "Sam Tell Difference": proactive customer service backed by a century of combined experience, tailored attention for each unique operation, and a culture that hires only passionate industry professionals. Those principles echo the founding values of dependability, integrity, and honesty that guided the original father-and-son team.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Commercial kitchen design", "Equipment installation and project management", "Foodservice equipment distribution", "Restaurant smallwares supply", "Shipping and delivery (tri-state and nationwide)", "Kitchen build-out and construction coordination"], "industries": ["Restaurants & Bars", "Sports & Entertainment Venues", "Hospitality", "Corporate Dining", "Healthcare", "Education", "Country Clubs", "Retail", "Airport & Travel Lounges"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": [], "facts_used": ["Founded 1956 by Sam Tell and Neil Tell -> /about", "Family-owned, three generations (Marc Tell grandson) -> /about", "180 employees, two Long Island warehouses, Manhattan showroom -> /about", "30th largest foodservice equipment and supplies distributor in US -> /about", "Services: design, build, supply; award-winning design team, skilled installers -> /about and /", "Industries served: restaurants, sports venues, hospitality, corporate dining, healthcare, education, country clubs, retail, airport lounges -> / and /about", "Chef Josh Capon testimonial for Lure Fishbar -> /", "Sam Tell Difference: proactive service, tailored attention, culture -> /about", "Shipping & delivery tri-state and nationwide -> /"], "company_type": "Distributor / reseller", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "The Sam Tell Companies is one of the largest restaurant and foodservice equipment and supplies dealerships in the nation.", "founded_year": "1956", "employee_count": "180", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "e