idence": "Tom''s is a state-of-the-art auto recycling facility, located in Waterbury, Connecticut. Every part of each car we dismantle is recycled or reused in an eco-friendly manner.", "founded_year": "1985", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='tom-s-foreign-auto-parts' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Tone''s Spices operates from Ankeny, Iowa, where the company was founded in 1873 by brothers Jehiel and Isaac Tone. What began as a spice and coffee venture grew into what the brand describes as the oldest spice company in the United States, remaining under the stewardship of the Tone family for generations.

The company manufactures a wide range of spices and seasoning blends — including garlic pepper, Cajun, Italian, lemon pepper, and taco blends — at a facility it characterizes as one of the largest spice production plants in the world. In 1888, the Tone brothers introduced individual pre-ground spice packaging, a shift that moved the industry away from bulk barrels and toward the consumer-ready format common today.

