UPDATE companies SET description='Tony''s Parts operates from Harrington, Delaware, where it was founded in 1977 by Tony D''Agostino. The business began as a part-time venture when D''Agostino sold surplus parts from a 1970 GTX to fund his own Road Runner restoration, eventually growing into a full-time operation with two large warehouses and a stock of donor vehicles.

The company specializes in new old stock (NOS) and used parts for Plymouth and Dodge muscle cars built between 1962 and 1974. It maintains an extensive inventory across its two warehouses and provides technical assistance and parts identification services. While Tony''s Parts once manufactured select reproduction components, those items are now distributed through Vans Auto.

Customers range from hobbyist enthusiasts to professional restorers. The company''s parts have been featured on the television series Graveyard Carz, and D''Agostino has contributed technical articles to publications such as Mopar Muscle, High-Performance Mopar, and Mopar Action.

Tony''s Parts distinguishes itself with a no-hassle return policy, a 100% refund guarantee on all sales, and a practice of referring customers to alternative suppliers when a needed part is not in stock. The founder''s decades-long immersion in the Mopar community and his published expertise underpin the business''s reputation.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["NOS parts sourcing and sales", "Used parts sourcing and sales", "Technical support and consultation", "Parts identification assistance"], "industries": ["Classic car restoration", "Automotive aftermarket parts", "Muscle car restoration", "Mopar enthusiast market"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Competitive pricing and no-hassle return policy", "100% refund on all parts sold", "Technical assistance and parts identification for customers", "Extensive inventory of NOS and used parts for 1962\u20131974 Mopar models", "Two large warehouses housing parts and donor vehicles"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1977 by Tony D''Agostino -> /about", "Located in Harrington, Delaware -> db", "Two large warehouses and donor vehicles -> /about", "NOS and used parts for 1962\u20131974 Mopar models -> /", "100% refund policy -> /about", "Technical assistance offered -> /about", "Featured on Graveyard Carz -> /about", "Articles in Mopar Muscle, High-Performance Mopar, Mopar Action -> /about", "Reproduction parts now via Vans Auto -> /", "Competitive pricing and no-hassle return policy -> /", "Dealer of choice for enthusiast and professional restorer -> /", "Tony D''Agostino is owner -> /about", "Started with 1970 GTX parts -> /about"], "company_type": "Distributor / reseller", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "Tony''s Parts is a Mopar-only dealer of NOS and used parts for classic muscle-era Mopar cars.", "founded_year": "1977", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='tony-s-mopar-parts-parts-for-60s-70s-plymouth-dodge-muscle-cars' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
