UPDATE companies SET description='Tricol Biomedical, Inc. is headquartered in Portland, Oregon, where it was established in 2001 as a U.S. corporation. The company originated from battlefield needs, partnering with the U.S. Army to create the first advanced hemostatic dressing for soldiers suffering traumatic injuries.

The company develops, manufactures, and markets a range of hemostatic and wound-care products built on its proprietary chitosan technology, branded as Chito+. Its product lines include HemCon® dressings for trauma management, OneStop™ devices for procedural care, and ChitoGauze® bandages for consumer self-care. Tricol operates as a fully integrated medical device company, handling research, development, and production in-house.

Tricol serves military, pre-hospital, and hospital markets, with documented use by U.S. Special Operations forces, emergency physicians, dialysis centers, oral surgeons, and general consumers. The HemCon bandage has been deployed in combat zones since 2003 and is also used in civilian settings such as cardiac surgery, vascular procedures, and home first aid.

The company''s stated vision is to achieve zero preventable deaths due to blood loss. Founded on the premise of saving and improving lives, Tricol''s mission centers on innovation in hemostasis, driven by its battlefield origins and a commitment to advancing the standard of care in bleeding control.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Chitosan-based hemostatic dressing manufacturing", "Medical device product development", "Wound care technology research and development", "Regulatory-compliant medical device production", "Hemostatic product formulation using proprietary Chito+ chitosan", "Trauma management product design", "Procedural care device engineering", "Consumer first-aid product manufacturing"], "industries": ["Trauma management", "Procedural care", "Consumer self-care", "Military/defense", "Pre-hospital care", "Hospital care", "Dialysis", "Oral surgery", "Emergency medicine"], "materials": ["Chitosan", "Chito+ proprietary chitosan"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Proprietary chitosan technology (Chito+) that binds to negatively charged tissues to promote rapid hemostasis", "Battlefield-proven HemCon\u00ae dressings, first advanced dressing used in combat for hemorrhage control (2003)", "Fully integrated medical device model covering R&D, manufacturing, and commercialization", "Partnerships with medical device companies to embed hemostasis solutions into their interventions", "Product portfolio spanning trauma management, procedural care, and consumer self-care"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters in Portland, Oregon -> db", "Founded in 2001 -> /about", "U.S. corporation incorporated in Oregon -> /about", "Proprietary chitosan technology Chito+ -> /", "HemCon bandage first advanced dressing used on battlefield 2003 -> /about", "Partnership with U.S. Army in 2001 -> /", "Product lines: trauma management, procedural care, consumer self-care -> /", "Used by U.S. Special Operations, emergency physicians, dialysis centers, oral surgeons -> /about", "Vision: zero preventable deaths due to blood loss -> /", "Mission: saving lives through innovation in hemostasis -> /about", "Develop, manufacture, and market hemostatic technologies -> /about", "Acquired full HemCon product line in 2016 -> /about"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Tricol Biomedical is a fully integrated medical device company dedicated to significantly advancing the standard of care in hemostatic and wound-care management.", "founded_year": "2001", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='tricol-biomedical-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Tropical Assemblies Inc operates from a facility at 4066 NE 5th Avenue in Fort Lauderdale, Florida. The company’s founding year and ownership structure have not been disclosed publicly.

The company provides electronic manufacturing services (EMS) with a focus on high-complexity, high-reliability assemblies. Its capabilities span printed circuit board assembly, electro-mechanical integration, RF and high-frequency communications hardware, LED lighting electronics, and full box-build services. The firm describes its operation as a "Smart Technology Factory" with real-time data tracking and audited quality systems.

Tropical Assemblies serves the aerospace, defense, medical, communications, LED lighting, and industrial controls sectors. In aerospace, it produces electronics for commercial and military programs worldwide. For defense, it supplies circuit board and electro-mechanical assemblies to armed forces. Its medical work, compliant with ISO 13485, supports device pioneers globally. The communications practice specializes in RF/HF systems, while the industrial controls group brings combined hardware, software, and mechanical design to market.

The company highlights its recognition as a finalist for the South Florida Manufacturers Association’s 2020 Manufacturer of the Year award and emphasizes its certified quality standards—AS9100, ISO 9001, ISO 13485, ITAR registration, and UL certification—as core differentiators.', certifications=ARRAY['AS9100','ISO 13485','ITAR','ISO 9001','UL Certification']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["PCB assembly", "Electro-mechanical assembly", "RF/HF communications assembly", "LED lighting electronic assembly", "Box build / system integration", "Hardware design", "Software/firmware development", "Mechanical design", "Supply chain management", "New product introduction (NPI) support"], "industries": ["Aerospace", "Defense", "Medical", "Communications", "LED Lighting", "Industrial Controls"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["High-complexity, high-reliability electronic manufacturing", "Smart factory with real-time production data tracking", "Certified quality systems: AS9100, ISO 9001, ISO 13485, ITAR, UL", "Specialized RF/HF communications assembly expertise", "Finalist, South Florida Manufacturer of the Year 2020"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters: 4066 NE 5th Ave, Fort Lauderdale, Florida 33334 -> /", "Certifications: AS9100, ISO 13485, ITAR, ISO 9001, UL Certification -> /", "Market sectors: Aerospace, Defense, Medical, Communications, LED Lighting, Industrial Controls -> /", "Capabilities: PCB assembly, electro-mechanical assembly, RF/HF communications, LED lighting assembly, hardware/software/mechanical design, supply chain management -> /", "Team: David Parker (CEO), Alan Cooper (VP), Janet Cole (CFO), Peter Sandler (Senior Engineer), Ricardo Gomez (HR Manager), James Smith (CTO) -> /about-us", "Award: Finalist, South Florida Manufacturers Association 2020 Manufacturer of the Year -> /", "Company description: ''Providing Next Generation of Advanced Electronic Manufacturing Services'' -> /"], "company_typ